---
import LegalPage from '~/components/site/LegalPage.astro';
import { brand } from '~/data/site';

const app = 'https://omninoise.multnelis.org';
const repo = 'https://github.com/cuongtranba/omninoise';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Omninoise"
  metaTitle="Omninoise: schedule your videos and posts to every platform"
  description="Omninoise is a publishing app from the multnelis team. Creators use it to schedule videos and image posts to TikTok, YouTube, Instagram, Facebook and Threads from one calendar."
>
  <p>
    Omninoise is a web app from the multnelis team for creators who publish the same work on several platforms. Connect
    your accounts once, upload a video or a set of images, and schedule it for each platform from one calendar.
  </p>
  <p><a href={app}>Sign up at omninoise.multnelis.org</a>. It is free.</p>

  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Connects your TikTok, YouTube, Instagram, Facebook and Threads accounts.</li>
    <li>Lets you write one post and adjust its caption and settings for each platform before it goes out.</li>
    <li>
      On TikTok, you choose who can see each post from the options your account allows, decide whether others can
      comment, duet or stitch, and disclose promotional content. Nothing is sent to TikTok until you press Post.
    </li>
    <li>Keeps your drafts and lets you move posts on the calendar.</li>
    <li>Shows each post’s status once it is published, and its views and likes where the platform provides them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Platforms</h2>
  <p>
    TikTok and YouTube are open to every account. For now, Facebook, Instagram and Threads work only for accounts the
    team has added.
  </p>

  <h2>Your accounts and data</h2>
  <p>
    Omninoise stores the access tokens each platform issues and the media you upload. It uses them only to publish your
    posts and to show how they perform. Disconnecting an account, or removing the app in the platform’s settings, stops
    Omninoise from using it. Delete your Omninoise account, or email us, and your data is deleted within 30 days. The
    details are in the <a href="/omninoise/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, and the rules for using the app are in the <a
      href="/omninoise/terms">Terms of Service</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Open source</h2>
  <p>Omninoise is open-source software under the AGPL-3.0 licence. The code is at <a href={repo}>{repo}</a>.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions, problems or deletion requests: <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
